{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>וַיִּתֵּן ה׳.</b> He said <b>בְּיָדֵנוּ</b> ('into our hand'). It may be explained along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory, in the chapter הרואה (Berakhot 54b) — that he uprooted a mountain-hill three parasangs and carried it on his head, and so on; Moses, how much was he, and so on; a bull, and he struck it with his ankle and killed it — end of quotation. And this is what the verse says, <b>וַיִּתֵּן ה׳</b> — meaning, by means of driving the mountain into his neck. And he says <b>בְּיָדֵנוּ</b> because they killed him with their actual hand, and it speaks in the plural just as in (Genesis 1:26) ״נַעֲשֶׂה אָדָם״; moreover, the hand of Moses is counted as the hand of all Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Aramaic quotations are from the Talmudic passage in Berakhot 54b about Og king of Bashan; rendered the summary phrases hyper-literally as they stand, without expanding the narrative."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:37.055629045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}